WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.592
Begin in the private welcome page, then
enter your workspace. This recording uses

00:00:05.592 --> 00:00:11.184
the real interface with disposable synthetic
data. Choose English or French and a

00:00:11.184 --> 00:00:17.260
comfortable theme. You can pause this guide,
change playback speed and turn captions off

00:00:17.260 --> 00:00:19.400
without changing the narration.

00:00:20.201 --> 00:00:25.999
Open Readiness before a new task. Read the
individual checks and their explanations,

00:00:25.999 --> 00:00:31.176
including local inference, document
isolation and recovery prerequisites. A

00:00:31.176 --> 00:00:36.767
responding service is useful evidence of
availability at this moment; it does not

00:00:36.767 --> 00:00:41.876
establish that every workflow is correct or
that recovery has been tested.

00:00:42.692 --> 00:00:47.464
Choose a mission that matches your work:
incident investigation, platform

00:00:47.464 --> 00:00:53.281
engineering, security or architecture. Write
the observed symptoms, their time window and

00:00:53.281 --> 00:00:58.510
any known changes. Keep client work in a
separate private environment and remove

00:00:58.510 --> 00:01:01.517
secrets from the request before submitting
it.

00:01:02.332 --> 00:01:08.077
Finally, inspect the runbook library. Read
the actual source content and check its

00:01:08.077 --> 00:01:13.751
relevance to your situation. The same
control API is available from the terminal.

00:01:13.751 --> 00:01:19.075
Start with the status and readiness
commands, and keep the interface open to

00:01:19.075 --> 00:01:21.807
review progress, sources and decisions.
